                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 39,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 582.0 ],
                                    "text": "Dynamics3 — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/dynamics3/\n\nWhat it is: a 2-in-1 downward expander / compressor built on quadratic\nBezier curves: the curve is literally a Bezier interpolation, re-solving\neach sample, so it reacts like a baked-in continuous curve rather than a\nculled/interpolated conventional attack-release engine. Very clean, very\n\"stealth\" sounding. This RNBO port uses the original normalized 0..1 values.\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_thresh (Thresh) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Blend/expander-compressor knee-ish intensity. Internally bezThresh =\n  pow(p+0.618)^2 * 1.618 (quadratic taper, i.e., it moves a lot at the top\n  of the scale). At the default 1.0 the plugin effectively bypasses\n  (bezThresh > 4.236): 1.0 = OFF. Lower values engage it; around 0.6-0.75\n  is a gentle setting, near 0.0 the most aggressive.\n\n- p_attack (Attack) 0..1, default 0.382 (golden-section default)\n  Control-response rate, NOT ms. Internally bezRez = pow((1-p)*0.4, 4) per\n  sample, i.e. a very steep exponential taper: high attack numbers are\n  dramatically slower, and each 0.1 near 0.0 matters a lot more than near\n  1.0... in practice lower p = faster response. The stair-step is hidden by\n  Bezier smoothing, so it never sounds steppy.\n\n- p_release (Release) 0..1, default 0.618\n  Same taper family as Attack for the floor/undershoot (sloRez =\n  pow((1-p)*0.4,4)); lower p = faster release of the curve baseline.\n\n- p_invwet (Inv/Wet) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Direction selector blended with dry/wet. Above 0.5 the module is a\n  compressor, below 0.5 a downward expander. The distance from the 0.5\n  midpoint also blends in dry signal: 0.5 = flat-ish dry, 1.0 or 0.0 = full\n  compressor / full expander. Default 1.0 = full compressor.\n\nMusical notes: typical use is p_thresh 0.7-0.8 as a \"transparent glue\"\ncompressor or a subtle expander on vocals/bass; the Bezier path makes\ndeep settings surprisingly clean but hints of over-realness (\"controlled\"\nsound) can appear at extreme depths.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
