                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 29,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 398.0, 438.0 ],
                                    "text": "PaulWide — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/paulwide/\n\nWhat it is: not a conventional stereo widener. It is a dither/decimation\nstyle stereo decorrelator: it quantizes audio with randomly dithered, NOT\ncorrelated dither between channels, at an adjustable bit depth. The\ndecorrelated dither acts as constant tiny uncorrelated signal, which the ear\nperceives as extra width and air (and a bit ofcontrolled \"air\"/level lift).\nThis RNBO port uses the original normalized 0..1 values.\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_quant (Quant) 0..1, default 1.0 (2 discrete modes)\n  Base processing depth, two discrete picks:\n  p_quant >= 0.5  24-bit processing (highres, internal scale 2^23)\n  p_quant <  0.5  16-bit processing (internal scale 2^15) - the original\n                  PaulWide behavior: noisier, wider character\n\n- p_derez (DeRez) 0..1, default 0.0\n  Progressive bit-depth reduction. Internally scale factor is multiplied by\n  pow(1-p, 6) (a steep curve: heavy settings already fall away quickly).\n  At low values it just adds the widening dither; as it nears ~0.4-0.6 it\n  sounds like lo-fi 8-4bit noise; near 1.0 it collapses nearly to noise\n  floor. Works on any program; use an ear.\n\nMusical notes: useful as a subtle air/width enhancer on the master buss (a\nlittle DeRez with Quant=24) or as a lo-fi crackle texture on a return. The\n\"widening\" is pure psychoacoustics from the dither, so high DeRez values\nshould be saved for effect use.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
