                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 39,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 582.0 ],
                                    "text": "PurestSquish — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/purestsquish-vst/\n\nWhat it is: the \"Purest\" family compressor: 5th-pass mu-style gain cell\nsimilar to VariMu's but tuned to be maximally clean and organic. It is\ndesigned as a 2-buss compressor with built-in auto makeup gain and a special\n\"bass bloom\" (BassBlm) feature: bass is pre-highpassed for the detector so\nlow frequencies are compressed less aggressively while still sounding full.\nThis RNBO port uses the original normalized 0..1 values.\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_squish (Squish) 0..1, default 0.0\n  How hard the gain cell squashes. Internally threshold = 1.01 - (1 -(1 -\n  p/2)^4): the full range endpoint is around 1.01; the top 10-20% of the\n  knob is where the really hard squish lives. Default 0 = only the\n  base-signal path (near-bypass, but not exactly full bypass).\n  Guides: 0.3-0.5 gentle leveling; 0.7-0.9 a heavy transparent squash;\n  past 0.9 the internal makeup gain becomes extreme (designed for the\n  hardest 2-buss use).\n\n- p_bassblm (BassBlm) 0..1, default 0.0\n  Bass bloom. An iirAmount = p^4 / sampleRate highpass: increases\n  non-linearly, dramatically more effective toward 1.0. When cranked it\n  lets the low end bloom out of the compressed signal (kick/bass\n  interactions get extra weight while staying controlled). For use on the\n  2-buss or a group: small values already make the low end feel fuller.\n\n- p_output (Output) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Linear output trim (unity at 1.0). The auto makeup gain is inside the\n  algorithm, so use Output for level-matching, not density.\n\n- p_drywet (Dry/Wet) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Linear dry/wet blend.\n\nMusical notes: start Squish 0.4 on a drum buss, then raise BassBlm until\nthe kick \"carries\" hard while the snare stays forward. The makeup gain is\nnonlinear (that is the whole character), so watch your level meters when\npushing Squish past 0.8.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
