                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 60,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 885.0 ],
                                    "text": "RCInflator2 (Ideal Edition) — RCJacH / sai'ke / chmaha (ReaTeam JSFX)\nPage: https://github.com/ReaTeam/JSFX/blob/master/Distortion/RCInflator2_Ideal.jsfx\n(REaPack distribution: ReaTeam JSFX -> Distortion, \"RCInflator2 (Ideal\nEdition)\". This is a free JSFX re-implementation of the classic Sonnox\nOxford Inflator algorithm for REAPER, reworked here as an RNBO codebox.)\n\nWhat it is: an Inflator-style loudness enhancer: a curve-controlled\nwaveshaper that lifts perceived loudness, warmth and density without\ncrushing dynamics, with an optional band-split for bass-safe processing\n(nonlinear saturation is split off the low end) and optional ideality\n(no \"positive clipping\"). This RNBO port keeps the source's parameter\nvalues (slider units). Note: \"Effect In\" bypasses only the waveshaper -\ninput/output gains and input clipping stay in the path (README note).\n\nParameters (original names):\n\n- input_db (Input) (dB) -6..+12, default 0\n  Input level before the waveshaper. Higher = more material hits the\n  curve boost, i.e. hotter into saturation. Negative = push right\n  down to keep the curve gentle for busy masters.\n\n- effect  (Effect) 0..100, default 0\n  The main Inflator amount: 0 = (quiet) exact bypass of the curve,\n  50 = classic moderately strong densify, 100 = the characterful\n  \"fully inflated\" curve. Raising it is almost always audible\n  immediately: richer low-mids and a warm, \"louder-feeling\" mix.\n\n- curve  (Curve) -50..+50, default 0\n  Waveshaper curve shape. -50 = most linear/natural (flattest curve,\n  gentle stuff), +50 = most aggressive \"compressed mid\" bulge of the\n  gain curve. The peak of the curve is around 0, so breaking out of\n  \"flat\" quickly gets characterful; common pro settings keep curve\n  <= +25.\n\n- clip  (Off/On enum) default Off\n  Input clipping toggle: when enabled, the input stage can hit the\n  ceiling like a real converter - adds its tiny extra compression\n  on loud material. Leave off for pure Inflator curves.\n\n- band_split (Off/On enum) default Off\n  Turns on band splitting (the source stays with the original\n  240/2400 Hz crossover, README note) so bass notes bypass the\n  waveshaper, avoiding the famous Inflator \"pumping bass\" effect.\n  On = safer for bass-heavy masters, slightly less glued together.\n\n- effect_in (Off/On enum) default On\n  Engages the waveshaper block itself. When off only the waveshaper is\n  bypassed - gains and input clipping are still in the path (README\n  note), so use it as a \"curve toggle\" for direct comparison.\n\n- output_db (Output) (dB) -12..0, default 0\n  Output trim, only attenuator (no gain up) - the source's output is\n  attenuator-only by design, so use Input and Effect to build level.\n\nMusical notes: the classic mastering chain is Effect 30-50, Curve\n0..25, band_split on for bass-heavy programs, then output trim to\nmatch. Beware: the perceived \"louder\" is largely psychoacoustic -\nA/B with level matched, and you'll find that your old \"hot\" settings\noften just rounded off the highs.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
