                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 63,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 928.0 ],
                                    "text": "TakeCare — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/takecare/\n\nWhat it is: a huge modal / delay-network wash (18 lines of 32767-sample\nmemory each, about 4.5 MB). It is not a conventional \"reverb\" but a very\nlong, very generative reverberant machine that behaves like three chained\necho arenas with vibrato, sample-rate slop (\"Derez\") and a householder-style\nfeedback. Sounds like a game-space of a fantasy cathedral AND like an\nold-school analog delay rack. This RNBO port uses the original normalized\n0..1 values and preserves all 18 x 32772 delay cells.\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_speed (Speed) 0..1, default 0.15\n  Vibrato speed of the whole wash. Internally vibSpeed = p^5 * 0.1, a very\n  steep fifth-power taper; the last 20% of the knob changes the speed far\n  more than the first 80%. Slow settings are \"tape-like\" drift; fast\n  settings get chorous-y and detuned.\n\n- p_rando (Rando) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Randomization of the vibrato phase/velocity per cycle. Internally\n  p^3 * 0.99 (cubic): at 0 it is a deterministic vibrato, at high values\n  each cycle gets a fresh randomized speed - the fuzz/growl of the space.\n\n- p_depth (Depth) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Vibrato depth as a fraction of the buffer length. Internally p^2 * 0.5\n  (quadratic): 0 = frozen (a long metallic delay), 0.5+ deeply smeared\n  modal washes. One of the two big \"mood\" controls.\n\n- p_regen (Regen) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Feedback into the lines. Internally p_regen * 0.0625 (max ~ -18 dB per\n  pass). Linear: at 0 the tail decays almost immediately; at 1 it is an\n  endless self-sustaining wash. Be careful: from ~0.8 upward tails get\n  visually \"stuck\" and can build to clipping (the module does not clip,\n  it just gets loud).\n\n- p_derez (Derez) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Internal sample-rate style darkening (\"tape slop\") across the whole\n  wash. Internally p*2 gives a 0..2 range folded around the 1.0 midpoint:\n  below 0.5 (of p) it is an undersampled/smoothed dark-down state, above,\n  up to 1.0, it becomes \"stepped\" (Stillair/-like stepped quantization with\n  the Bezier undersampling). Default 0.5 is a musical middle ground.\n\n- p_buffer (Buffer) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Basic delay length of the arenas. Internally targetBuf = p^3 * 32510 +\n  256 samples: at 0 = tiny (256 samples), at 1 = 0.74 s at 44.1 kHz.\n  Steep cubic taper - the first 50% of the knob only doubles the size.\n  Tails run longer with bigger buffers.\n\n- p_output (Output) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Linear output trim (unity at 1.0). Because of the long feedback, always\n  listen-from-quiet when experimenting with Rando/Regen extremes.\n\n- p_drywet (Dry/Wet) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Wet is internally 1 - (1-p)^2 (a soft \"more/less\" curve). Note the port\n  preserves the source's signed wet output: p_drywet 0 passes dry audio\n  only (after the source's near-1-second ramp) - it does not make a hard\n  bypass in the middle of a tail.\n\nMusical notes: use it as a do-everything \"space\" on a reverb return. Give\nit time to develop (the 32767x18 state fills gradually); trial Buffer\nvalues at 0.1, 0.4, 0.7 to hear three different \"rooms\". For the classic\nairy \"fog horn\" sound: Regen 0.6-0.7, Depth 0.5, Derez 0.3, Rando 0.3.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
