                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 29,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 396.0, 438.0 ],
                                    "text": "TapeHack2 — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/tapehack2/\n\nWhat it is: a minimalist tape-style soft-saturator. Instead of trying to be\nconventional \"hysteresis\" tape emulation, TapeHack2 hits a soft saturation\npoint, flattens the top (smoothly) and darkens the quiet parts, using a\nleveled cascade of \"dark\" averaging filters. Sounds like a recording\nconsole put into a mild analog clip. This RNBO port uses the original\nnormalized 0..1 values.\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_input (Input) 0..1, default 0.1\n  Drive into the saturator. Internally a gain of p*10, i.e. x10 (+20 dB)\n  at max; the default 0.1 is already a mild drive. Relentless attention:\n  even small pushes add real loudness, so do A/B at equal levels.\n\n- p_output (Output) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Output trim. Internally multiplied by 0.9239, so a small RTA-like loss is\n  baked in by the source; 1.0 is the calibrated setting.\n\n- p_drywet (Dry/Wet) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Linear dry/wet blend.\n\nMusical notes: use it on a single track (vocals, drums, bass) it adds a\nsmeared-edge analog vibe; on a buss at the default 0.1 drive it is a\nsubtle \"warmer\" glue. Beware of turning Input all the way up: it does NOT\nsound merely \"louder\", it adds real harmonic distortion and darkens\ntransient bite. Set level by Output.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "lines": [
                            {
