                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 41,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 611.0 ],
                                    "text": "VariMu — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/varimu-vst/\n\nWhat it is: an airwindows-style Vari-Mu (variable-mu tube-style)\ncompressor: the gain cell is a muVary function with a variable slope curve,\ncontrolled by a fixed threshold, with a smoothed sliding release. It is a\n5th-family Airwindows compressor: clean, musical, with automatic makeup\ngain and no ratio/pump controls, purely driven by the \"mu\" physics.\nThis RNBO port uses the original normalized 0..1 values.\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_intensty (Intensity) 0..1, default 0.0\n  Effectively the compressor's threshold via the threshold variable\n  threshold = 1.001 - (1 - (1-p)^3): the cubic taper puts nearly all of\n  the action in the top 30% of the knob. Small values (0..0.2) hardly slow\n  anything down (near-bypass, included auto makeup); values 0.6+ are the\n  sweet zone; 1.0 is extreme limiting. Automatic makeup gain is included\n  in the output mapping at all settings.\n\n- p_speed (Speed) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Release time. Internally release = pow(1.15-p, 5) * 32768 / overallscale,\n  then divided down for the two sliding speed histories. That makes a very\n  steep curve: at p=1.0 release is almost instantaneous; at 0.0 it is\n  several seconds long. Default 0.5 is roughly a medium-fast program\n  release. This is \"release character\", not literally calibrated meters.\n\n- p_output (Output) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Output trim on top of the automatic muMakeupGain (which is calculated\n  from Intensity, so Incre\n\nase actually becomes louder as you compress):\n  output = outGain * p_output.\n\n- p_drywet (Dry/Wet) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Linear dry/wet blend.\n\nMusical notes: the classic Airwindows \"nothing to see here, sounds like a\ntape buss\" compressor. Typical master-buss use: Intensity 0.6, Speed 0.5,\nOutput 1.0. Because of the nonlinear makeup curve, watch your ears/buss\nlevel as you push Intensity; set level with Output afterwards.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "lines": [
