                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 40,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 597.0 ],
                                    "text": "VerbThic — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/verbthic/\n\nWhat it is: the sibling of VerbTiny: the same 5 controls, but the opposite\ncharacter. Where VerbTiny is thin, airy and \"tssshhh\" (spaciousness),\nVerbThic's specially evolved matrix is dense, thick and soupy, for adding\nbody and weight to sounds rather than depth of space. Use it to make pads,\nsnares or vocals fat without buying tubes. This RNBO port uses the original\nnormalized 0..1 values.\n\nParameters (identical layout to VerbTiny, different delay network):\n\n- p_replace (Replace) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Regeneration (\"Galactic-style replace\" in the feedback path). This matrix\n  rings denser than VerbTiny: the same values read as \"heavier\" and stay\n  dense further up the knob. Push high for thick endless washes, watch\n  saturation at the top end.\n\n- p_derez (Derez) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Bezier undersampling / darkening of the wet. Higher = cleaner; lower =\n  progressively duller and more \"lo-fi early reverb\" character.\n\n- p_filter (Filter) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Wet tone via Bezier filter. 1.0 = brightest; lower = rounder, duller,\n  like a blanket over the plate. In VerbThic it also sort of thickens when\n  darkened (dark low end stays big).\n\n- p_wider (Wider) 0..1, default 0.0\n  Same tri-mode wideness as VerbTiny: normal stereo near 0, weird dual-mono\n  blending near 0.5, hyper-wide opposite-phase near 1.0. On such a dense\n  matrix the differences are subtler - it reads more like \"thickness\n  location\" than space effect.\n\n- p_drywet (Dry/Wet) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Normal linear dry/wet blend (1.0 = full wet return).\n\nMusical notes: the counterpart room-mate of VerbTiny. Use VerbThic on\nthings that need mass (cymbals, pads, snares) and VerbTiny for air on a\nsmall budget. As always on Airwindows verbs, full tails develop over 2-3\nseconds - trust your ears after a while, not the first 500 ms.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
