                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 50,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 741.0 ],
                                    "text": "ZAcidLowpass — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/zacidlowpass/\n\nWhat it is: the \"acid\" member of the Z filter family: a resonant lowpass\nbuilt from Bezier undersampling plus an Emu e6400-style output clipping\nstage, plus an unstable \"meltdown\" control that feeds the raw audio into\nthe filter's control voltage path. It is a filter-meets-ring-modulator\nexperiment; the resonance is nasty in a good way. This RNBO port uses the\noriginal normalized 0..1 values and keeps the fixed 15.5 kHz op-amp HP/LP\nfilters - so use sample rates ABOVE 31 kHz (README note).\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_cutoff (Cutoff) 0..1, default 0.5\n  Filter frequency, but with a cubic taper: internally pow(p, 3) scaled to\n  sample rate, so most of the musical range (about 100 Hz - 15 kHz for\n  typical SR) lives in the top half; the bottom third is extremely low.\n  A resonant-sounding lowpass through the Bezier curve, not a biquad.\n\n- p_over (Over) 0..1, default 0.0\n  \"Over\" behavior: together with Under it makes a sort of crossover. With\n  Over only, tones above the cutoff are passed and boosted  (a peppy\n  YAHTC-like resonant filter that pushes highs). With Meltdown combined it\n  becomes the MOST aggressive: with Over at 1 and Meltdown at 0 you get\n  the famous \"crazy overtones and harsh noise\" setting. Linear 0..1.\n\n- p_under (Under) 0..1, default 1.0\n  The complementary half of the \"crossover\": Under is the passive lowpass\n  accent. Over + Under both at 1 near the midpoint approximates the plain\n  resonant lowpass; Over alone is a distinctly gritty highpassed tone.\n\n- p_meltdwn (Meltdown) 0..1, default 0.0\n  Feeds the raw (pre-filter) audio directly into the control voltage path\n  instead of the averaged/darkened one: more aliasing, chaos, and\n  ring-mod-flavored artifacts. Linear; moderate values already sound\n  \"broken\".\n\n- p_drive (Drive) 0..1, default 0.1\n  Input trim into the Z-style distortion stage. Internally a fourth-power\n  mapping: (p*10)^4, from about x1 at 0.1 up to x10000 (+80 dB!) at 1.0 -\n  a very steep taper with enormous range, designed for abuse. Default\n  0.1 is roughly unity.\n\n- p_output (Output) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Output pad before the fixed 15.5 kHz stage. Linear trim.\n\nMusical notes: works as a real acid box: Cutoff + Resonance-taste, then\npush Drive and Meltdown for industrial textures; or with Over for\nhighpassed stabs. Because of the fixed 15.5 kHz filter, do NOT use\nlow sample rates (README note above).\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
