                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 34,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 510.0 ],
                                    "text": "ZOutputStage — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/zoutputstage/\n\nWhat it is: the output clipping/tone stage shared by the Emu e6400-flavored\n\"Z\" filters, as a standalone saturator: an insane-degree.input-staged\nfourth-power gain trim into a k-style soft clipper, followed by fixed\n15.5 kHz op-amp-style ultrasonic filters. Cleaner and simpler than\nZAcidLowpass: no filter, no resonance, just the Z distortion/tone stage.\nThis RNBO port uses the original normalized 0..1 values and the same fixed\n15.5 kHz filters, so use sample rates ABOVE 31 kHz (README note).\n\nParameters:\n\n- p_input (Input) 0..1, default 0.1\n  Drive into the Z distortion stage. Internally (p*10)^4, so 0.1 is\n  roughly unity and the same DRIVE mapping as the Z filters, for x10000\n  (+80 dB) at max - huge, steep taper. Start at or below the default and\n  raise slowly.\n\n- p_output (Output) 0..1, default 1.0\n  Output pad (outPad = p_output, linear). Use it, not Input, to set\n  final level after the distortion.\n\nNo other parameters:\n\n- (none)\n  Fixed internal 15.5 kHz ultrasonic filtering (two biquads) rooms out\n  the floppy aliasing the distortion would otherwise generate. This is\n  the \"weight/tone\" family smell of the Z filters, not a mix knob.\n\nMusical notes: use on single tracks (bass, drums, synths) as an aggressive\nsaturator that you can push from subtle to wildly broken. Because the\ninput mapping is fourth-power, small moves near the default have large\naudible effect - push gently and A/B at equal levels with Output.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
