                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 45,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 669.0 ],
                                    "text": "GateIQ 0v2 — mrelwood plugins\nPage: https://mrelwood5.wixsite.com/plugins\n(GateIQ has no individual page on the site; it is listed under Gain in the\nmrelwood plugin list and ships inside the free mrelwood_PluginPack.)\n\nWhat it is: a smart 4-band downward gate/expander. Each band's detector\nweaks and releases per band with a \"smart release time\" based on the\nsignal frequency. In this RNBO port the active band gain is applied\nTWICE to the signal (intentional, matching the source), and the input is\nsummed to MONO when the gate is active - with threshold at -96 dB (the\nlowest position) the module simply passes stereo through untouched\n(README notes). Read-only meter sliders of the source are omitted.\n\nParameters (original names):\n\n- slider1 (Threshold) (dB) -96..-6, default -45\n  Gate threshold in dBFS; -45 is the reasonable \"gate everything below\n  this\" position. -96 is special-cased: it bypasses the gate effect\n  while staying stereo (see above). -6 is the most aggressive.\n\n- slider2 (Range) (dB) 0..48, default 20\n  The maximum depth of the gain reduction once a band closes. 0 = no\n  reduction (band stays open), 48 = almost a utility mute. 15-25 dB\n  keeps things \"lungingly musical\", 48 is heavy noise-floor gating.\n\n- slider4 (Threshold Hi, dB) -12..+12, default 0\n  Per-band detector threshold offset on top of the main threshold, for\n  the HIGH band. Positive = that band triggers at a higher level\n  (gates less often); negative = more likely to gate.\n\n- slider5 (Threshold High Mid, dB) -12..+12, default 0\n  Same style of band offset for the high-mid band.\n\n- slider6 (Threshold Low Mid, dB) -12..+12, default 0\n  Same style of band offset for the low-mid band.\n\n- slider7 (Threshold Low, dB) -12..+12, default 0\n  Same style of band offset for the low band. Typical use: push the\n  lows a bit negative so kick/bass floors stay open even when the\n  top end closes.\n\nPort quirks (README notes): the twice-applied band gain when the gate is\nactive is deliberate and matches the JSFX source; threshold -96 dB\n(stereo bypass) is likewise preserved, NOT replaced with an on/off\nswitch. The smart release times of the source are retained.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
