                                        ],
                                        "helpname": "loadmess",
                                        "aliasOf": "loadmess",
                                        "classname": "loadmess",
                                        "operator": 0,
                                        "versionId": -361086158,
                                        "changesPatcherIO": 0
                                    },
                                    "text": "loadmess 0",
                                    "varname": "load_slider62"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 79,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 1158.0 ],
                                    "text": "Sky is the Limit 3.2 BETA — mrelwood plugins (Sky Limiter family)\nPage: https://mrelwood5.wixsite.com/plugins/sky\n(Individual page is for the Sky 2.05 release; the 3.2 BETA ships inside\nthe free mrelwood_PluginPack. Port keeps the source's own slider names.)\n\nWhat it is: mrelwood's master limiter, built around a smart combination\nof lookahead/instant limiting, tiltable saturator, pre-compression and\n\"safe vs soft clip\" character. It is designed to push a master's RMS\nunrealistically high without audible distortion, or to replace a chain of\ncompressors/maximizers. This RNBO port preserves the source's initially\nzero limiter histories; slider51/53/62 exist but are inert in the audio\nequations (source behavior, README note) and lookahead CPU cost can be\nhigh with higher slider51 settings.\n\nParameters (original names):\n\n- slider1 (Mid/Side) 0..1, default 0.2\n  0 = stereo processing, 1 = mid/side. Low default means most behavior\n  happens in plain L/R and mid is only slightly different - the \"2.0\"\n  behavior keeps this three-way rather than a hard switch.\n\n- slider2 (Link L/R, M/S) 0..1, default 0.2\n  Detector linkage between channels. At 0 the two channels' limiters\n  run independently; at 1 they are totally linked (no image shift but\n  less \"pumping\" character). Musically: small values keep natural\n  stereo dynamics, high values make pumping key off the louder of the\n  two pans.\n\n- slider5 (Tilt EQ) -6..+6, default 0 dB\n  Pre-limitation tilt shelves (Sky's characteristic tilt EQ). Positive =\n  brighter master, negative = darker. Not a full EQ - keep 1-2 dB.\n\n- slider6 (Pre Compression Punch) 0..1, default 0\n  Pre-compression stage that adds punch before the limiter. 0 = off;\n  values above 0.3 start to bring out the transient \"bite\" the\n  limiter would otherwise shave off. For extreme nothing.\n\n- slider7 (Pre Saturation) 0..1, default 0\n  Pre-saturation before the limiter. Small doses warm up the signal so\n  the limiter has less work to do; high values cause more harmonic\n  densifying. Start with 0.1-0.2 on a quiet master.\n\n- slider10 (Limiter / Boost dB) 0..30, default 0\n  The total loudness gain the limiter is allowed to apply. 0 = no\n  limiting; 6-12 dB is the normal working area for a punchy master;\n  20-30 dB is deliberately destructive \"crunched\" territory.\n\n- slider11 (Safe vs Soft Clip) 0..1, default 0.2\n  Character of the final over-shoot treatment: 0 = \"safe\" (keeping\n  overshoots mild) to 1 = full soft-clip curve saturation. With the\n  source's slider62 inert, changing this just picks the final shelf's\n  equation. Small values feel master-safe, edging past 0.7 gets\n  distinctly warmer/dirtier.\n\n- slider51 (Look ahead, ~5 ms) 0..1, default 0\n  Lookahead window, internally up to 256 scan cells per active detector\n  per sample - CPU cost scales steeply (README note). 0 = instant\n  limiting (zero latency, aggressive clipping), higher = softer,\n  more program-identifying but slower, and the audible latency is\n  bufsz - 1 samples.\n\n- slider53 (Pre comp) 0..1, default 0\n  NOTE: exists in the source UI but does NOT affect the active audio\n  equations in this version (README note). Whether it becomes active\n  in a later release is mrelwood's call.\n\n- slider60 (Ceiling) -18..0 dB, default -0.1\n  Absolute output ceiling. -0.1 dBFS is standard; -1..-6 are safe\n  choices for loudness-normalization-friendly masters. Keep ceiling at\n  least ~1 dB below 0 to avoid encoder overshoots.\n\n- slider62 (Link Threshold & Volume) 0..1, default 0\n  Same situation as slider53: kept for source parity, inert in the\n  audio path.\n\nMusical notes: for a punchy master, Slot 10 to 6-10 dB, slider6 at 0.3,\nTilt about +1, Ceiling -1 dB, and choose Safe/Soft around 0.3. When the\nmaster pumps, lower slider6 first - a louder-transparent master isn't\njust about maximizing the boost knob.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
